  "body": "## Summary\n\nConditional \u03ba = **0.001661956299899884** (conservative 0.001661956297017522). This is +7.60\u00d710\u207b\u2079 over the U8 package (research/gauge44-barch, 0.001661948695165034).\n\n**Change: FanPUYen's PR858 sixteen-replica owner controller, applied to the U8 word.** PR858 (closed, unmerged) introduced a controller with 16 data replicas in two 8-replica parent bank groups (144 invocations), plus 11 whole-helper owner edits that turn idle remainders (44,3,3) into (48,2,0). U8's owner map is the same file as PR799's, so PR858's edits apply verbatim to the U8 word. Prefix 401 \u2264 512 bits; row coefficient 16,469 \u2264 20,161; deficit 5,120.\n\n**Code:** U8's reviewed code plus PR858's edits applied verbatim, plus one glue edit (72\u2192144 in freeze_spec). `t16/build_owners.py`, `build_parent.py` and `source_adapters.py` are byte-identical to PR858, and `t16/MOVES.json` is exactly PR858's 11 edits. The new `verify_t16.py` runs every check of the 8-replica `verify_global.py` (69 admission, 12 bit-supplier and 6 independent controls) plus PR858's owner audit, its 11 omitted-move controls, the changed-role count, bank-group accounting, literal windows, the prefix and coefficient limits, and all of PR858's final-binding asserts.\n\n**Independent review: SOUND.** The reviewer rebuilt every changed code file from U8 plus PR858's edits (all matched), reproduced the strict run, and confirmed that a wrong owner move, a wrong offset, an omitted move, a bank-group overlap, a window-violating move and a 513-bit prefix overflow are each rejected end-to-end.\n\n## Verification\n\nFrom a fresh clone of commit b734850d (Windows, CPython 3.11.11), using U8 locals rebuilt from scratch by the U8 chain (the clean replay of research/gauge44-barch above):\n- `verify_manifest.py`: PASS, 152 files\n- `verify_t16.py`: **PASS_GAUGE44_T16_STRICT_GLOBAL_REPLAY 0.001661956299899884**\n\n## Credits\n\n- **FanPUYen** (PR858): the sixteen-replica controller, owner edits and adapters, used here verbatim.\n- **NewBArch** construction and everything credited in research/gauge44-barch.\n\nConditional on PR645's premises and PR589's bit-supplier assumptions. No optimality is claimed for sixteen replicas.\n\nPrepared with Claude Code (Anthropic).\n",
